1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:18,685
Next job: the Ortiz kitchen, with a blind corner, a filler and finished end panels.

2
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:26,779
The left wall starts with a finished end panel at its open end...

3
00:00:26,779 --> 00:00:31,401
...then a 24" base.

4
00:00:31,401 --> 00:00:39,114
The corner is a 36" blind corner base: a 24" blind part hidden behind the next run.

5
00:00:39,114 --> 00:00:52,928
Along the back wall: the 36" sink base, a 24" base, an 18" drawer base...

6
00:00:52,928 --> 00:01:00,787
...and another end panel to finish the right end.

7
00:01:00,787 --> 00:01:12,364
Site measure: the back wall is 121", the left wall 96".

8
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:19,817
Arrange: the blind corner sits in the back-left corner, pulled out from the left wall for its door.

9
00:01:19,817 --> 00:01:24,459
The left run butts against the blind corner's face. The end panels finish both open ends.

10
00:01:24,459 --> 00:01:27,582
The back run is short of the wall, and the app says by how much.

11
00:01:27,582 --> 00:01:32,207
Fill gap adds one filler of exactly that width (Split would put half at each end).

12
00:01:32,207 --> 00:01:35,141
The run now meets the wall. The filler is a cabinet of its own, F1.

13
00:01:35,141 --> 00:01:39,358
Elevation of the back wall: blind corner, sink, bases, filler and end panel in one line.

14
00:01:39,358 --> 00:01:51,346
In 3D you can see the toe-kick notch on the end panels.

15
00:01:51,346 --> 00:02:06,742
The Cut list: end panels, the filler and the blind corner's parts are all here.

16
00:02:06,742 --> 00:02:11,912
Hardware is totalled at the bottom: Salice hinges and 3 mm plates, TANDEM slides.

17
00:02:11,912 --> 00:02:19,319
Nesting puts the whole kitchen on 5 x 12 ft sheets.

18
00:02:19,319 --> 00:02:26,811
The Output tab checks the job before anything goes to the machine. Output switches stay off.

19
00:02:26,811 --> 00:02:29,812
A blind corner, a filler and two end panels, fitted to the wall in a few clicks.
